# Git & Polyrepo

- Mainline: `master <- stage <- develop`.
- Features: `feature/fix(<number>)/<slug>`.
- Commits: `<seq:03d>-<brief-kebab-title>` (example `001-add-health-endpoint`).
- Backends: `service-<intent>`; frontends: `ui-<context>`.
- Working copies live under `<workspace>/repos/<name>` (hub-relative path `../repos/<name>` in `project.yaml`).
- Hub `scaffolds/` are molds only; after INSTALL, implement in `repos/`.
- This hub orchestrates; each product folder under `repos/` is its own GitHub repository.
- Subagents: each owns commit + push on the feature branch.
- Orchestrator: residual commit for leftovers (hub and/or remaining repo files).
- Before coding: create the feature branch from `develop` in the impacted repo under `repos/`.
